@startuml
title Launch Manager - Run Target Transition Failure

autonumber "<b>[00]"

participant "StateManager" as sm
participant "Launch Manager" as LM
participant "OS (kernel)" as kernel
participant "random" as ran
participant "app1" as app1

activate LM
activate sm

note over LM
Current Run Target: "Minimal"
Components StateManager and setup_filesystems.sh are Ready.
end note

=== Transition from "Minimal" to "Running" ==

sm -> LM : Activate Run Target ("Running", forced=False)
LM --> sm : Request accepted
LM -> LM : Determine transition plan from "Minimal" -> "Running"

group #White Start random
    ref over LM, ran
        Activation of Component random.
        See Run Target Activation sequence diagrams for details.
    end ref
    activate ran
    LM -> LM : Component random Ready
end group

group #Pink Start app1
    loop up to the configured activation attempts for app1
        LM -> kernel : Start app1
        kernel -> app1 ++ : Start app1
        app1 -> app1 : Initialization
        LM -> LM : Wait for app1 ready condition\n(Process reported 'Running')

        alt #Pink app1 crashes during initialization
            app1 -> kernel : exit
        else #Pink app1 does not report Running within the configured ready timeout
            LM -> app1 : SIGTERM (escalation to SIGKILL after shutdown timeout)
            app1 -> kernel : exit
        end alt

        deactivate app1
        kernel -> LM : app1 terminated with error
        LM -> LM : Activation attempt for app1 failed
    end loop

    LM -> LM : All configured activation attempts for app1 exhausted,\nComponent app1 activation failed
end group

LM -> LM : Transition to Run Target "Running" failed
LM -> LM : Remove any queued requests (here: none are queued)
LM -> LM : Determine Run Target Recovery Action configured for Run Target "Running"


note over LM
The only supported Run Target Recovery Action is the activation
of the Fallback Run Target, here Run Target "Fallback".
end note

=== Transition to "Fallback" Run Target ==

LM -> LM : Determine transition plan from current state -> "Fallback"

note over LM, app1
Run Target "Fallback" only depends on Component StateManager, which is already Ready.
app1 was never activated and therefore stays deactivated.
random is not part of Run Target "Fallback" and is therefore terminated.
end note

group #White Deactivate app1
    note over LM
        The underlying process for app1 is already in state terminated. No further action required.
    end note
    LM -> LM : Mark Component app1 as Terminated
end group

group #White Stop random
    LM -> ran : SIGTERM
    alt random terminates within the configured shutdown timeout
        ran -> kernel : exit
        destroy ran
        kernel -> LM : random terminated successfully
    else #pink random does not terminate within the configured timeout
        LM -> ran : SIGKILL
        ran -> kernel : exit
        destroy ran
        kernel -> LM : random terminated with error
    end alt
end group

LM -> LM : Run Target "Fallback" successfully activated
LM -> sm : Invoke callback: Run Target "Fallback" activated\ndue to Run Target Recovery Action

...
@enduml
